INT. FUNICULAR CAR - ALPINE CLIMB - NIGHT

A glass cabin crawls up a mountain in the dark, a cable humming overhead and the lights of a casino resort burning at the summit like a held breath.

SABINE LACROIX (30s, black gloves, a champagne flute she hasn't touched) sits with her back to the glass. Across from her TEODORO "TEO" BIANCHI (40s, bow tie loose, a briefcase cuffed to his wrist) stares at the floor. A figure in a gray coat leans in the corner, face lost in the shadow of a hat: THE MAN IN GRAY.

From a speaker above the door, a bored VOICE of the operator drones through the static.

OPERATOR (V.O.)
Next stop, Summit Station. Please remain seated until the car has come to a complete halt.

SABINE
Fourteen minutes. The vault door cycles at the quarter hour. Teo takes the case through the service lift, I take the lobby, and our friend in gray makes the cameras blink.

TEO
You say that like it's simple.

SABINE
It is simple. It's only terrifying.

THE MAN IN GRAY
My cameras blink for ninety seconds. Not ninety-one.

SABINE
Then we move in eighty.

TEO
And if the guard on the service lift is the new one? The one who doesn't take bribes?

SABINE
Then Teo recites the wine list until he cries.

TEO
That is not funny.

THE MAN IN GRAY
Halvard.

SABINE
What?

HALVARD
My name. If we're doing this, you should have it. Halvard.

SABINE
Halvard. Fine. Eighty seconds, Halvard.

OPERATOR (V.O.)
Summit Station in one minute.

TEO
One minute.

SABINE
Breathe, Teo.

HALVARD
Gloves on.
